  "notes": [
    "Irregular -AR verb with an accent shift: the *i* in the stem takes a written accent (*í*) and carries the stress in every form except nosotros/nosotras — same pattern as *enviar*, *confiar*, *vaciar*, *guiar*",
    "Not a stem-vowel change in the e→ie/o→ue/e→i/u→ue sense, so no stem-change tag applies — just an orthographic stress shift",
    "Past participle: *desviado* (regular)",
    "Means \"to divert\" or \"to deflect\" — *desviar el tráfico* (to divert traffic), *desviar la atención* (to deflect attention)",
    "Reflexive *desviarse* means \"to go off course\" or \"to get sidetracked\": *nos desviamos del camino* (we strayed from the path)",
    "Related: *desvío* (detour, diversion), *desviación* (deviation, detour)"
  ],
